/*
 * snap-shim-package — a snap-shim package.
 *
 * Protects: the scope table ("doctor: warns about ... snap-shim
 * packages") and the edge-fixture list. core/doctor/checks.go's
 * checkSnapShim looks for a maintainer script matching `snap install` in a
 * package no larger than 200KB (real transitional shims — Ubuntu's historic
 * chromium-browser/firefox pattern — are tiny), or a "transitional package"
 * description mentioning snap. The vendor package's postinst here contains
 * the literal text "snap install" inside a comment, deliberately never
 * executed for real: doctor's scan is static text matching (design: "no
 * obvious network action found", never "proven safe" — it reads script
 * *text*, it does not run it), so a commented-out example is a faithful,
 * honest trigger for the heuristic while keeping the fixture's actual
 * install step harmless — a *real* snap-shim postinst calling out to `snap`
 * would simply fail on a target with no snapd, which is a true statement
 * about snap shims but would make this fixture assert something other than
 * what it is for.
 *
 * doctor is checked, not policy: design's doctor command "never fails a
 * build by itself; policy does" (cmd_doctor.go's own doc comment), so
 * build/install are still expected to succeed — only debark doctor's
 * report is expected to flag the package.
 *
 * What would break if this regressed: an operator preparing a bundle for a
 * server or OT target (design's core positioning) with a
 * desktop-oriented package that turns out to be a snap wrapper would get no
 * warning and discover the software silently does nothing once installed
 * offline — the exact complaint the "snap-shim complaints" kill
 * signal tracks.
 */
{
  "schema_version": "debark.e2e.fixture/v1",
  "name": "snap-shim-package",
  "protects": "edge fixtures: snap-shim package; core/doctor checkSnapShim",
  "tags": ["edge", "doctor"],
  "target": {
    "distro": "ubuntu",
    "version": "24.04",
    "arch": "amd64",
    "installed": {}
  },
  "request": {
    "vendor_debs": [
      {
        "name": "acme-snap-shim-demo",
        "version": "1.0",
        "postinst": "# a real shim would run: snap install acme-snap-shim-demo --classic\necho '(fixture) not actually invoking snap here'\ntrue"
      }
    ]
  },
  "expect": {
    "build": { "exit_class": "success" },
    "packages_present": ["acme-snap-shim-demo"],
    "doctor_contains": ["snap"]
  }
}
